# Spend skill ranks on skills chosen BY NAME, and photograph the result.
#
# This is the check behind @cursorto:mark (bd inc-cso). The Skill Manager has
# no menu letters at all -- it is a scrolling list with a '>' beside the
# current row (src/Managers.cpp:1664) -- so until now the only way a script
# could reach a skill was to count DOWN keystrokes to it. A skill added to
# lib/, or a character with a different class list, moved every count after
# it, and the script then spent the ranks somewhere else and still finished.
#
# WHY THESE NINE SKILLS. They all sit late in the list, and the positional
# script this one is derived from (tools/keys/chargen-rogue.keys) reaches only
# the first nine: Alchemy through Diplomacy. So the assertion is not merely
# "the ranks were spent" -- it is "the ranks were spent where no amount of
# counting from the top would have put them". tools/check_key_directives.sh
# checks both halves: these nine carry ranks, and Alchemy carries none.
#
# The names are given in list order because DOWN does not wrap here: the
# Skill Manager stops at the end of the list (src/Managers.cpp:1713-1720)
# rather than returning to the top, so @cursorto:mark can only walk forward.
#
# Nine skills at a maximum of two ranks each is exactly the eighteen an elf
# rogue starts with, and character generation will not let go while any rank
# is unspent.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
@choose "Neutral"
a                       # First feat
a                       # Second feat

@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"

@cursorto:mark "Listen" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Lockpicking" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Perform" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Pick Pockets" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Ride" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Spot" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Tumble" DOWN
RIGHT*3

ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes
a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
d       # character sheet
@expect "Race   Elf"
W                       # Write Dump
s h e e t ENTER         # filename: "sheet"
@dump:afterdump
ESC
@quit
